WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:15.750
- [Mark] Okay, Lindsay.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:16.970
Lindsay, where have you been?
- [Lindsay] Yes.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.090
- [Mark] I've been looking for you for

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:22.090
like almost three weeks
now since we last spoke.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:24.150
And you disappeared from Hollywood.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.440
- Yeah.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.273
I went to jail.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.193
- [Mark] You were in jail?
- Yeah.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.350
I--
- [Mark] Can you just be

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:34.100
really brief about what for?

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.660
I don't need all the details.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.493
- Yeah.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.100
Assault with a deadly weapon.

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:41.100
- [Mark] Assault with a deadly weapon.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:41.933
- Yes.

00:00:43.286 --> 00:00:46.210
I mean, I went into Popeye's,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.823
and put a knife to somebody's throat.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:54.010
- [Mark] Why did you do this?

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:59.010
- I was, honestly coming off of drugs and,

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:00.580
I drank a little bit of alcohol.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.640
Then I got angry because, nobody loves me.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:05.913
I thought that nobody
loved me, but Ben does.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.790
His daughter does and.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.530
- [Mark] And about
300,000 that my viewers.

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.430
(laughter)
- Yes.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:14.643
Yeah.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.590
Thank you guys for all
the comments anyways.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.150
- [Mark] Yeah, she just got out of jail.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.197
- Yeah, I haven't been able to read 'em.

00:01:20.197 --> 00:01:23.100
- [Mark] You just got to jail
just, minutes ago, right?

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.400
- Yeah.
- [Mark] Ben and I helped.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.860
Ben is an old friend of yours?

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:26.693
- Yeah.

00:01:26.693 --> 00:01:28.610
- [Mark] Who I've never met, but he,

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.610
he called me out of the blue and said...

00:01:31.832 --> 00:01:32.665
You know, I talked to him.

00:01:32.665 --> 00:01:33.770
He saw the video and said,

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:36.660
and then I've also been
speaking with your mom

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.986
over the last couple of weeks.

00:01:37.986 --> 00:01:39.319
- How'd that go?

00:01:40.610 --> 00:01:41.740
- [Mark] Very well, I mean very nice.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.600
I mean, she,

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:45.900
we're all kind of on a similar page that,

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.410
you know, it seems to me like your

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:49.033
medication is a big part of,

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:51.573
some of your problems.

00:01:52.515 --> 00:01:53.550
- Yes.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.730
- [Mark] And if you don't
take them, things go haywire.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.213
- Yeah.
- [Mark] It sounds like.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:01.477
- Yeah, pretty much I mean...

00:02:01.477 --> 00:02:03.013
- [Mark] You would agree with that?

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.560
- Yeah.
- [Mark] It's a common story--

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.540
- Yeah, I would.
- [Mark] Down here.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.110
'Cause a lot of the people I'm talking to,

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.080
we wanna blame the drugs.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.100
But honestly, the problem
is more of a mental problem.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.170
They're not taking their
medications so they end up taking,

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.840
then they take drugs and then
it looks like a drug problem

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:19.011
but it's honestly a mental issue.

00:02:19.011 --> 00:02:23.493
- Yeah.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:28.320
- [Mark] So you've been in
jail for almost three weeks?

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.470
- Mm hmm.
- [Mark] Two and a half weeks?

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:32.690
- Yeah.
- [Mark] And, how was that?

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.250
- Jail sucks.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.563
It's very cold, in the suicide dorm.

00:02:38.710 --> 00:02:39.960
They ignore you.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:40.870
Well, they ignored me.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.703
They wouldn't,

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:44.283
give me a grievance or,

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:51.603
a medical paper to speak to the doctors.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:56.210
They make it very cold
in the room when they,

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:57.860
whenever I told 'em I was anemic.

00:03:03.130 --> 00:03:07.890
They, mistreat you very
bad in the dorm 1202.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.313
1201's not so bad.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:14.760
But 1403 is the mental place.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:15.920
I was supposed to get my clothes back

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.830
but they never gave 'em back to me.

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.883
Don't know why but, whatever.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:34.030
I mean, a lot of stuff escalated
towards me going to jail.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:35.533
Like, almost being raped.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:43.463
I kinda, almost did get raped, actually.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.150
If I wouldn't have put my
knee up against his chest

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:48.370
and pushed him off and then just like

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.790
clocked him in the head,

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.330
he wouldn't have, and then screamed,

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.903
he wouldn't have left me alone.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:03.970
I stayed in a tent with a
guy that was going to hurt me

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:08.757
because, he had a knife and I said,

00:04:08.757 --> 00:04:09.590
"Hey, can I

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:14.940
can I hold your knife because
something don't feel right."

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.163
So he gave me his knife.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:20.130
That night, he went to sleep
and I stayed up all night.

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.800
If I hadn't have had that knife,

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:24.010
this guy would've came in and hurt us

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.700
because this guy that I didn't know,

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.330
poked his head in the tent.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.587
And I swamped, I switched out
the switchblade and I said,

00:04:29.587 --> 00:04:30.960
"Get the fuck out."

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.100
And, he got pissed off.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:38.100
So he took all the money by
the door of the tent and left.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:39.700
And then whenever my friend woke up,

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:40.640
I told him what happened.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.940
And he was mad because
all the money was gone.

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:50.453
- [Mark] Life on the
street is, crazy like that.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.147
- Yeah, it is crazy.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:04.170
The same guy, whenever I
try to get away from him,

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.480
before, when he had his knife

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:08.790
which led up to this story
that I just told you,

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:11.300
this little tidbit that I just told you,

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:15.870
he, I tried to get away
from him one night.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.220
And I was walking Hollywood Boulevard

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.600
tryna stay on camera, tryna stay in sight.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:22.460
I went into, in front of the
cameras of Hard Rock Cafe.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.780
I went in front of every
camera that I could find,

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:26.610
and he was following me so I had to like,

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:29.110
keep a good eye out on him and,

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.463
change sides of the street.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.440
I got away from that.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.970
And then I took his knife.

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:42.310
- [Mark] And this happened the night after

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:43.540
you and I spoke, right?

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:44.390
- Yeah.
- [Mark] The same day?

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:45.530
- Oh yeah.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.893
Well, no, actually.

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:51.230
Wait, yes.

00:05:51.230 --> 00:05:52.063
Yes, it did.

00:05:52.063 --> 00:05:53.143
- [Mark] I think it was.

00:05:54.293 --> 00:05:55.610
According to your mom.

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:56.870
- I'm sorry?
- [Mark] According to your mom

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.370
'cause she had the date
of the arrest and then

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.647
I looked at the data of
video, it's the same day.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:03.950
- Yeah.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:05.560
My mom doesn't know anything about

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.860
how I'm doing out here
other than through Ben.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.863
I wish she'd just leave me
the fuck alone, honestly.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:17.400
I really do.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.380
Yeah, I'm fucking sick of her

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:21.290
stalking me and trying to find
out everything, little bitty,

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:22.940
every little thing about my life.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:26.523
Mom I'm fucking sick of you,
leave me the fuck alone.

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:33.670
- [Mark] What would you like
to see happen for, Lynne?

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:34.503
Like from here on out?

00:06:34.503 --> 00:06:35.336
- Me?
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:06:35.336 --> 00:06:37.070
- I would love to just
like, maybe go to rehab,

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.420
get a social worker,

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:41.270
get my own place and start my life.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:43.900
That's what I would like to see happen.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:46.200
I mean, I would go to
rehab because, you know?

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.905
People can't just stop
thinking about drugs.

00:06:49.905 --> 00:06:52.610
You just, don't stop
thinking about it, you know?

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:54.573
You gotta go to rehab and get help.

00:06:54.573 --> 00:06:55.710
- Yeah, I think there were actually

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.030
quite a few comments from

00:06:58.290 --> 00:07:00.740
people that run rehabs and therapists

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.460
and all kinds of people that

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:05.093
offered up their services to you.

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:08.023
So maybe on this video, we can kinda,

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:10.623
get in touch with some of those people.

00:07:13.211 --> 00:07:15.878
(deep exhaling)

00:07:19.996 --> 00:07:23.618
(scratching sounds)

00:07:23.618 --> 00:07:26.240
What do you think the chances
are of you sticking with a

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:27.500
recovery program and just

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:30.200
following through?
- The chances of that

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.183
are very good.

00:07:32.740 --> 00:07:34.790
Because I feel I need it.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:36.030
- [Mark] That's great,
are you clean right now?

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.500
'Cause you've been in
jail for three weeks.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:38.550
- Yeah, I am.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.320
I mean, would I go back
out there and do drugs?

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.120
No, but I still think I need rehab.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.360
- [Mark] Yeah, no I--

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:45.240
- In order to get a social worker.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:46.690
In order to get my own place.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.033
The night that,

00:07:53.033 --> 00:07:55.410
actually, the same day
that you gave me the

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.320
money for the previous interview.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.153
- [Mark] Yes.

00:07:59.270 --> 00:08:01.290
- I went to buy alcohol with it.

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:04.603
And I was in a frantic
mindset because nobody,

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:08.340
like I said, nobody gave a shit about me.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:09.173
So,

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.790
I tried to buy alcohol and I accidentally

00:08:13.790 --> 00:08:16.460
tried to buy it with my
food stamps card one time.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:17.860
And then I accidentally tried to buy it

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:19.570
with my social security one time.

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:20.870
Because I never have cash.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:22.820
I never had money in hand.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.873
So I'm not used to having money in hand.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.271
- [Mark] Well, Ben seems
like a good friend.

00:08:37.271 --> 00:08:38.104
- He is.

00:08:41.008 --> 00:08:42.710
- [Mark] He's gonna let you
stay with him for a few days,

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:43.543
at least?

00:08:43.543 --> 00:08:45.580
- Hopefully my court date's tomorrow.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:46.660
- [Mark] Oh, your court date's tomorrow?

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:47.980
- Yep.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.730
- [Mark] Well, it's good that you're out.

00:08:49.730 --> 00:08:50.870
- Yeah.
- [Mark] I think--

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.543
- I mean right now, I
think all I need to do is,

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.300
well, all I want to do right now,

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.300
'cause I don't know how jail's gonna go.

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:02.653
I just wanna smoke a blunt and eat.

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.140
And just chill in a bed.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.240
That's all I wanna do.

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:12.510
- [Mark] You could probably
do two or three of those.

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:13.343
Maybe all three.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:15.470
At Ben's, I'm sure.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:17.183
- Hopefully.

00:09:24.208 --> 00:09:26.410
I wanna go back to Hollywood.

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:27.678
- [Mark] You wanna go back to the streets?

00:09:27.678 --> 00:09:28.511
- Not in the streets.

00:09:28.511 --> 00:09:29.880
I just wanna walk around
the Hollywood Boulevard.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:30.747
- [Mark] Oh, okay yeah.

00:09:30.747 --> 00:09:32.030
Well that's,

00:09:32.030 --> 00:09:34.980
as long as you don't end
up in the same kind of...

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:36.360
- As long as I'm not
there in the nighttime,

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:37.787
I think I'll be all right.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:40.730
Because it gets cold at night.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.940
And I'm anemic, so I can't
really just sleep on the streets

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:46.937
with no blanket.

00:09:46.937 --> 00:09:47.770
- [Mark] Mm hmm.

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:50.580
- I have to be in a
tent or have a blanket.

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:52.580
Or walk around all night
and deprive myself of sleep

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:53.930
and maybe sleep in the sun.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.600
But that's what the
bracelets in jail look like.

00:10:11.900 --> 00:10:12.733
- [Mark] How?

00:10:12.733 --> 00:10:14.020
So how, tell me about jail.

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:15.220
What was the worst part?

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:18.840
- I think the worst part was

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:20.853
being cold and being mistreated.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:26.260
- [Mark] And probably coming
off the drugs too, right?

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:27.630
- Yeah,

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:28.463
kinda, yeah.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.213
Yeah.

00:10:36.750 --> 00:10:38.520
- [Mark] You've been in jail before?

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:39.353
- Yes.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:41.783
- [Mark] And,

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:47.410
that time, was it also like
your medications might've been

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:49.050
off or something you weren't taking

00:10:49.050 --> 00:10:50.900
that may have triggered that?

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:57.560
- The first time I went
to jail in Florida,

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.400
I wasn't on any medication.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.570
Actually, I would just come home drunk

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:03.560
and get something to eat
and try to go to my room.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.250
And my mom would aggravate me.

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.720
To the fullest extent.

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:09.100
To the point where I would throw my food

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.530
or yell or something because
I'm believe I'm autistic.

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:14.003
And she would, she never
leaves me the fuck alone.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:20.340
And then I get to call,
the cops called on me.

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.173
And then I'd go to jail

00:11:21.173 --> 00:11:22.350
just because she doesn't want me home

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:24.210
or she needs a break
or some shit like that.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:26.110
Instead of just telling me to get out.

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:29.880
- [Mark] She has a shed for you.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:32.890
So she showed me a picture
of, in her backyard.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.370
- Who, a shed?

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:36.213
- [Mark] Yeah.
- I'm not going back home.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.370
Why the fuck should I
have to stay in a shed?

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:43.042
Why can't I stay in the house, you know?

00:11:43.042 --> 00:11:44.960
- [Mark] I'm just, gonna

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.020
show you the message that
she wanted me to tell you.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:47.853
- Oh, okay.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.130
I mean, unless it's a brand new shed

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:52.240
and unless it's in my name,

00:11:52.240 --> 00:11:55.000
and unless I'm left the fuck alone, maybe.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.333
But other than that, no.

00:11:57.173 --> 00:11:58.006
- [Mark] Well, now that you're out,

00:11:58.006 --> 00:11:59.160
you guys can probably speak.

00:12:00.020 --> 00:12:01.793
- I don't know if I'll speak to her again.

00:12:05.270 --> 00:12:06.600
I might.

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:07.433
I don't know.

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.400
- [Mark] The rehab, you think is

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:15.600
what is it?

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:18.070
Is it the alcohol, is it
drugs, is it the whole thing?

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.193
Is it, tell me what you think is.

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.593
- Rehab, it's,

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:26.770
I don't know.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:28.540
I'll go for whatever they
think I need to go for.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.570
- [Mark] And then they'll
probably figure that out.

00:12:30.570 --> 00:12:31.403
- Yeah.

00:12:43.603 --> 00:12:47.290
I mean, Ben is nice enough
to let me stay with him, so.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:48.620
- [Mark] Yeah, he seems like a nice guy.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:49.980
- He is.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:52.000
